{"change_summary":"Implemented the pending carbon-guard remediation in `tank_core`. The hourly chemistry pass now has an explicit budgeted path that records the atmospheric DIC shortcut as a `system:chemistry` carbon `BudgetDelta`, with gross inflow/outflow terms clamped to available DIC so the explicit budget still reconciles to the state delta. `Engine` now uses that explicit chemistry budget only when tracking is enabled, preserving the zero-cost disabled path, and the runtime carbon guard no longer disables itself whenever chemistry moves DIC; it subtracts the known chemistry exchange and still flags unrelated carbon drift elsewhere in the same tick. Added engine-level guard regressions plus updated budget-tracking coverage to verify preset-like DIC exchange is explicitly tracked and does not suppress carbon-leak detection.","outstanding_risks":["The structural canonical-helper coverage guard is still convention-based rather than reflective; future explicit N/C-bearing fields with non-standard names or fields hidden in empty-by-default collections will require extending the discovery rules and tests.","Complex multi-process stages such as `system:nitrogen_cycle` still rely on snapshot-derived gross component budgets, so same-component turnover inside a single pass can remain collapsed until those stages emit fully explicit source/sink deltas.","The carbon guard now correctly subtracts the explicit `system:chemistry` atmospheric DIC shortcut, but any future open-system carbon shortcut introduced in a different stage will need the same explicit-budget treatment or the guard helper must be extended to account for it."],"steps":[{"description":"Audit the current tick-level carbon guard and chemistry-stage budget recording to confirm that non-zero `system:chemistry` DIC flux was suppressing runtime carbon enforcement for the whole tick.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Implement an explicit chemistry-budget path that records gross carbon inflow/outflow for the atmospheric DIC shortcut and wire `Engine` to use it only when budget tracking is enabled.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Replace the old carbon closed/open gating with a residual-based guard that subtracts the known chemistry exchange before checking for unexplained carbon drift, and add regressions covering both the pass and fail cases.","order":3,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Run formatting plus focused and full-package validation to confirm the new chemistry budget and carbon guard behavior do not regress `tank_core`.","order":4,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_tracking` passed (18 tests), including the updated preset-DIC regression that now verifies explicit `system:chemistry` carbon inflow/outflow without disabling the guard.","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed across the full `tank_core` suite, including the new engine unit tests proving chemistry flux does not open the carbon guard and that unrelated same-tick carbon drift still trips `SimError::BudgetImbalance`.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -- -D warnings` passed.","`cargo fmt --all` completed after the code changes."]}